Chapter: LeanSearchSpec
  cites Foreword chapter ListUtils
  cites Foreword chapter Console
  cites Safari chapter Geom
  cites Safari chapter Pose
  cites Safari chapter Bike
  cites Safari chapter World
  cites Safari chapter Arc
  cites Safari chapter LeanSearch
  cites Judge chapter Grade

 LeanSearch: bisect for the lean that puts the rider where he wants to be, by
 projecting a whole arc at each candidate.

 THE TARGET IS AN ASYMPTOTE AND NOT THE CENTRE LINE, which is the design decision
 this chapter turns on. He aims at a FRACTION of his current offset, so he
 converges on the middle without ever committing to a lean that overshoots it.
 Aiming at zero instead would be the obvious thing and would weave.

 DEAD CENTRE GETS A SIGNED EPSILON, because a target of exactly zero has no side
 to lean toward. The sign comes off the offset he already has, and `>= 0`
 means a rider at exactly zero leans one particular way rather than neither --
 graded from both sides of the boundary, since a `>` there would flip it.

 THE SEARCH IS TWELVE BISECTIONS OF A TWO-DEGREE BRACKET, so what can be asserted
 without re-deriving the arc is the bracket and its width: the answer is inside
 [tilt - 1 degree, tilt + 1 degree] and the twelve halvings have narrowed the
 interval to under a thousandth of a degree. That is the honest claim -- the
 VALUE it converges on is `project-arc`'s answer, and ArcSpec grades that.

 We say:

Section: The Target

 Beyond the epsilon he aims at three tenths of his offset; inside it he takes the
 epsilon itself, signed.

  target-got : List Real
  target-got =
    [ lean-target 0.5, lean-target (0.0 - 0.5),
      lean-target 2.0, lean-target (0.0 - 2.0),
      lean-target 0.04, lean-target (0.0 - 0.04),
      lean-target 0.0, lean-target 0.039, lean-target (0.0 - 0.039) ]

  target-want : List Real
  target-want =
    [ 0.15, -0.15, 0.6, -0.6, 0.012, -0.012, 0.04, 0.04, -0.04 ]

 The target always points the way he is already off, and never past the middle:
 a rider to the right is sent to a smaller positive offset, never to a negative
 one.

  side-got : List Boolean
  side-got =
    [ lean-target 2.0 > 0.0, lean-target 2.0 < 2.0,
      lean-target (0.0 - 2.0) < 0.0, lean-target (0.0 - 2.0) > (0.0 - 2.0),
      lean-target 0.0 > 0.0 ]

  side-want : List Boolean
  side-want = [True, True, True, True, True]

  tuning-got : List Real
  tuning-got = [asymptote-tuning, center-lane-epsilon, max-tilt-correction]

  tuning-want : List Real
  tuning-want = [0.3, 0.04, 0.017453292519943295]

  iters-got : List Integer
  iters-got = [lean-search-iters]

  iters-want : List Integer
  iters-want = [12]

Section: Reading An Arc

 The two shoulders answer without looking at anything else -- off the left means
 lean further right, off the right means do not -- and only the no-shoulder case
 consults the target. That short-circuit is the assertion: an outcome that left
 the road answers the same whatever its end-across says.

  outcome : Shoulder, Real -> ArcOutcome
  outcome (sh) (end-across) =
    ArcOutcome { shoulder = sh, forward = 10.0, crossed = False, end-across = end-across, frames = 100.0 }

  read-got : List Boolean
  read-got =
    [ want-more-right (outcome ShoulderLeft 99.0) 0.5,
      want-more-right (outcome ShoulderLeft (0.0 - 99.0)) 0.5,
      want-more-right (outcome ShoulderRight 99.0) 0.5,
      want-more-right (outcome ShoulderRight (0.0 - 99.0)) 0.5,
      want-more-right (outcome ShoulderNone 0.4) 0.5,
      want-more-right (outcome ShoulderNone 0.6) 0.5,
      want-more-right (outcome ShoulderNone 0.5) 0.5 ]

  read-want : List Boolean
  read-want = [True, True, False, False, True, False, False]

Section: The Search

  seg : Segment
  seg = segment-at 0

  rider : Real, Real -> RiderState
  rider (across) (tilt) =
    RiderState { segment = 0, along = 0.0, across = across, yaw = 0.0, v = v-base,
                 tilt = tilt, heading = 0.0, gaze-yaw = 0.0, focus = 0.0 }

 Whatever it converges on is inside the bracket it was given, which is one degree
 either side of the lean he is already holding.

  centred : Real
  centred = best-tilt-correction (rider 0.0 0.0) seg

  offset : Real
  offset = best-tilt-correction (rider 1.0 0.0) seg

  held : Real
  held = best-tilt-correction (rider 0.0 0.5) seg

  bracket-got : List Boolean
  bracket-got =
    [ centred >= 0.0 - max-tilt-correction, centred <= max-tilt-correction,
      offset >= 0.0 - max-tilt-correction, offset <= max-tilt-correction,
      held >= 0.5 - max-tilt-correction, held <= 0.5 + max-tilt-correction ]

  bracket-want : List Boolean
  bracket-want = [True, True, True, True, True, True]

 THE BRACKET IS CENTRED ON THE LEAN HE IS HOLDING, not on zero, so a rider
 already leaning half a radian gets an answer near a half rather than near
 nothing. That is what makes it a CORRECTION.

  centred-on-got : List Boolean
  centred-on-got =
    [ real-abs (held - 0.5) <= max-tilt-correction,
      real-abs centred <= max-tilt-correction,
      held > centred ]

  centred-on-want : List Boolean
  centred-on-want = [True, True, True]

 Twelve halvings of a two-degree bracket leave an interval under a thousandth of
 a degree, so the answer is determined to far finer than any lean the rider can
 see -- and calling it twice gives the same number, since nothing here is
 stateful.

  stable-got : List Real
  stable-got =
    [ best-tilt-correction (rider 1.0 0.0) seg - offset,
      best-tilt-correction (rider 0.0 0.5) seg - held ]

  stable-want : List Real
  stable-want = [0.0, 0.0]

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni (grade-reals "ls-target" target-got target-want 0.0)
    print-line-uni (grade-bools "ls-side  " side-got side-want)
    print-line-uni (grade-reals "ls-tuning" tuning-got tuning-want 0.0)
    print-line-uni (grade-ints  "ls-iters " iters-got iters-want)
    print-line-uni (grade-bools "ls-read  " read-got read-want)
    print-line-uni (grade-bools "ls-brackt" bracket-got bracket-want)
    print-line-uni (grade-bools "ls-centre" centred-on-got centred-on-want)
    print-line-uni (grade-reals "ls-stable" stable-got stable-want 0.0)
  end
